stimulus.description:
A website stores customer reviews in an ArrayList<Review>. The Review class and the header of the method you will write are shown.
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Review {
    private String text;
    private int stars;
    public Review(String t, int s) { text = t; stars = s; }
    public String getText() { return text; }
    public int getStars() { return stars; }
}

public class ReviewStats {
    /** Returns the average number of stars of the reviews whose text contains word,
     *  or -1.0 if no review contains word. */
    public static double averageFor(ArrayList<Review> reviews, String word) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static double averageFor(ArrayList<Review> reviews, String word) {
        int total = 0;
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < reviews.size(); i++) {
            Review r = reviews.get(i);
            if (r.getText().indexOf(word) >= 0) {
                total += r.getStars();
                count++;
            }
        }
        if (count == 0) {
            return -1.0;
        }
        return (double) total / count;
    }
```

