public class GridShift {
    /** Returns a new two-dimensional array with the same dimensions as grid in which each row of grid
     *  has been shifted one position to the right; the last element of each row moves to the front
     *  of that row. The array grid is not modified.
     *  Precondition: grid is rectangular and has at least one row and one column. */
    public static int[][] shiftRight(int[][] grid) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int[][] shiftRight(int[][] grid) {
        int[][] result = new int[grid.length][grid[0].length];
        for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
            for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
                result[r][(c + 1) % grid[r].length] = grid[r][c];
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
