import java.util.ArrayList;

public class RunFinder {
    /** Returns the length of the longest run of consecutive equal values in data.
     *  Returns 0 if data is empty. The list data is not modified. */
    public static int longestRun(ArrayList<Integer> data) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int longestRun(ArrayList<Integer> data) {
        if (data.size() == 0) {
            return 0;
        }
        int best = 1;
        int run = 1;
        for (int i = 1; i < data.size(); i++) {
            if (data.get(i).equals(data.get(i - 1))) {
                run++;
            } else {
                run = 1;
            }
            if (run > best) {
                best = run;
            }
        }
        return best;
    }
```

